WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.900
A Notice from the Yamayuri Council
When watching
"Maria Watches Over Us ~Printemps~,"
please have the room brightly lit and
sit well away from the television set.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.430
See you later!

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:20.940
See you later.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.700
I had anticipated to some
degree that this would happen.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.310
But even if it was anticipated,

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.570
when I'm faced with such outright opposition,

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.580
it's actually going to get
me more fired up about it.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:53.110
What?

00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:58.840
What did you just say?

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:01.720
So like, since we're in a new school year now,

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:04.160
I'm thinking about getting
involved with a club soon.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:09.160
What I'm asking you to
repeat is the part after that.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:09.930
The part after that?

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.370
I won't oppose you getting involved with a club.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.230
After all, you've been doing
well after the operation,

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:20.200
but...

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.140
But?

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.280
Of all the clubs out there...

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:26.850
The Kendo Team?

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:33.150
Is the problem because the Kendo Team
is known for how tough it is?

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.150
Or is it because it's the
club you're involved with?

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:37.950
Both.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:41.760
Then, even if I said I wanted
to join the Craft Club,

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.030
you'd be against it if you were in that club?

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.740
Pardon me, I'd like some water.

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:58.470
Please!

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:02.740
Don't ask for more water when we're
having a serious conversation!

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:06.720
Um, what shall I do about the water?

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:09.420
Please don't mind this one.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.190
"This one"?

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:23.400
"This one" is good enough for you
when you're being so ungracious.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.840
Am I behaving shamefully?

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:31.940
Yes.

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:35.340
It's really embarrassing to see you
behave flustered because of me.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.850
You want to do kendo, no matter what?

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:45.590
Yes, I'm thinking it might be good to do.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.590
You don't know how harsh sports teams can be!

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.260
We have morning practices!

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:54.660
And even in the winter, we have
to scrub the training hall floor!

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.870
We go barefoot all year round!

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.310
It would be a nuisance if you joined the team...

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:01.210
...based on some half-baked notion
that it "might be good to do"!

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.040
If it's a diversion to stave off boredom,

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.940
I'll keep you company at home!

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:07.440
A diversion to stave off boredom?!

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.950
You'll keep me company?!

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:10.140
No, thank you!

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:13.180
Rei-sama needn't go to such trouble!

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.380
Y-Yoshino...

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.120
This is bad. This pattern is...

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.860
Not good, not good.

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:27.930
I have to restrain myself. Restrain myself...

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:29.390
But...

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:32.810
Fine, then! If that's the case...

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:38.000
The rosary...

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.410
I forgot I'm not wearing it today.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:41.750
Yoshino...

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:43.550
I'm going home.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:04:00.300
Maria Watches Over Us
Printemps

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:09.570
In the morning mist,
Asamoya no naka

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:16.450
the white path goes on.
tsuzuku shiroi michi

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:23.950
The birds sing.
Tori no saezuri

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:31.620
We exchange greetings.
Aisatsu kawashinagara

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:39.070
At times, the clouds hang low,
Toki ni kumo ga tarekomete

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:46.580
and the sun may grow dim.
hizashi kagerou tomo

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:54.680
But I will walk with my chin up,
Sesuji nobashite aruku

00:04:54.760 --> 00:05:02.130
for I know,
watashi wa shitteru kara

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:09.130
that above those heavy clouds...
omoi kumo no ue wa

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:17.130
...is the blue sky.
aoi sora

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:23.880
Yellow Rose Weather Advisory

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:34.790
Was this path always this long?

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.800
Oh, right.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:40.730
It's because Rei-chan would
always talk to me the whole way.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.440
On days when I wasn't feeling well,

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:45.500
I guess she even carried my bag for me...

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:53.270
That's why it never felt long.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:56.210
Rei-chan...

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:01.650
What's with that sigh?!

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:04.350
Like she's the only one with troubles!

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.660
"Please make it so we can reconcile"...

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.830
I'm never going to wish for that.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:21.110
Even if I don't ask for it, I'll bet...

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:22.810
Later.

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:27.780
What was that?!

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:35.350
Yoshino-san?

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.050
Yumi-san

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:39.530
Good morning.

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:40.820
Is something wrong?

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.620
G-Good morning.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:44.960
No, just doing a little weather prediction.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.000
So what does it forecast?

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:51.300
Considering neither is upside down,
clear skies, I suppose.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:52.900
Clear skies?

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:58.070
I doubt it's going to clear up.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:06:59.970
Oh? How can you be so sure?

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:03.840
Because this won't do what I want it to.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:05.210
Meaning?

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:06.750
There's a lot of moisture in the air.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.150
In other words, I have a feeling
that rain is not too far off.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:12.230
That makes sense.

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:15.060
Yoshino-san, did something happen?

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:18.800
Nothing... really.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:22.540
Club Application
Year: 2 Class: Pine Name: Shimazu
I would like to join the Kendo Team,

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.040
Club Application
Year: 2 Class: Pine Name: Shimazu
I would like to join the Kendo Team,
I'm going to ask you, just in case,

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:24.560
I'm going to ask you, just in case,

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:28.970
but your request to join the Kendo
Team isn't as a manager, right?

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:33.170
No, I would like to wield
a bamboo sword and fight.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.150
I see.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:38.710
The Kendo Team, is it?

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:43.180
Are you against my joining the
Kendo Team as well, Hoshina-sensei?

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:44.550
Well, I suppose...

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:49.620
By the way, does Hasekura
Rei-san know about this?

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:54.330
Would it put your mind at ease if
Hasekura Rei said it was all right?

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:59.040
She's a special person to you,
in more ways than one.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.140
Am I wrong?

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:03.270
No...

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:10.910
Really, it's been a great help
to have you, Noriko-chan.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:12.980
I hope I have.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.650
You think so too, don't you, Yumi-chan?

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:17.610
Yes, of course!

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.160
We all think so.

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:24.260
What's with Rei-chan? Acting all smiley like that...

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:28.660
I see, so I don't figure into the picture. Is that it?

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:33.800
Isn't it great, Noriko?

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.000
Yes.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:39.240
Shimako-san and Noriko-chan
seem so fresh and innocent.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.580
I envy that...

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:48.080
Compared to that, we're...

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:51.950
...like a couple who's grown
weary of being married...

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:56.120
Maybe it wasn't such a good idea,
no matter what I thought,

00:08:56.460 --> 00:09:00.160
to have applied to join the team
without even letting Rei-chan know...

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:03.100
Maybe I'll go reconcile with her, after all.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:06.370
All right, I'll talk to her tomorrow.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.610
Come visit me sometime at the Kendo Team, too!

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:14.080
Even so, I think Rei-chan's being
excessive with the smiles.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.450
Maybe this is how life works...

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:28.690
Here I was, all ready to reconcile with Rei-chan,

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.760
but she didn't come to school today.

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:34.820
What? Rei-san is absent?

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:37.930
It seems she suddenly came down with a fever.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:40.100
Could it be... my fault?

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:42.870
Huh? Why would it be your fault?

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:46.100
I called Rei-san last night.

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:46.980
I see...

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:50.710
At first, I was telling her about what
happened with the team yesterday,

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:53.790
but the talk inadvertently turned to you, and...

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:58.260
In other words, she found out that
I had applied to join the team...

00:09:58.260 --> 00:09:59.750
...without letting her know about it.

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:02.260
That can't have been good, right?

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:04.920
No, she would have eventually found out anyway.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:08.670
But you know, the moment Rei-san
learned that you had joined the team,

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:10.690
she became speechless with shock.

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:15.700
But that makes it more my fault
than the team president's fault.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:19.510
Honestly! Just how frail can you be, Rei-chan?!

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:22.140
Uh, um, Yoshino-san?

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:23.250
Team President!

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:24.120
Yes?

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:26.610
I am joining the team, no matter what it takes!

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:32.990
Rei-chan isn't at school.

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:35.560
No one can stop me now!

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:38.670
Then, I will introduce you to the person...

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:40.220
...who will be mentoring you, starting today.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:41.730
I look forward to working with her.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:44.340
I look forward to working with you.

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:50.010
Tanuma Chisato-san?

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:54.280
Your hair...

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:58.110
I cut it. I find it refreshing.

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:00.650
I-I see...

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:04.290
Chisato-san, could I ask you something?

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:05.020
Go ahead.

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:07.550
Since when did you join the Kendo Team?

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.360
The end of our first-year.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:12.990
The end of our first-year would
put it right after that date.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.890
I suppose it does.

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:22.870
Yoshino-san, it's almost unbelievable
how inflexible you are.

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:25.670
You've never done any kind
of real exercise, have you?

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:27.550
Well, excuse me.

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:30.620
Owowow...

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:32.350
You shouldn't strain yourself.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:34.990
You'll have to begin by
building up basic strength.

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:36.290
Kendo isn't so easy...

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:38.880
...that you can start swinging a
bamboo sword around right away.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:40.250
Right, right.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.530
By the way, how is Rei-sama doing?

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:50.200
She seems to have a fever,

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.230
so she'll probably be absent for a couple days.

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:53.540
I see.

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:58.700
But I can't believe Rei-chan!

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:01.410
She never told me about Chisato-san!

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:03.450
Maybe it's because Chisato-san is here,

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:06.010
that she didn't want to
let me join the Kendo Team.

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:08.260
I know it's a mean suspicion to have, but...

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:09.310
Come on, put your back into it.

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:11.890
Owowowowowow!

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:18.690
Yoshino-san, how is the kendo going?

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:20.530
Well, it's coming along.

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:24.390
Yoshino-san, you don't look happy.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:30.440
Yumi-san...

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:34.550
I become blind to my surroundings
when I get absorbed in something.

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:37.380
Could it be that I've been offending people?

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:40.890
I've never felt that way myself...

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:46.280
Maybe I'll get myself a little sister.

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:49.060
How did this conversation
make the leap to that?

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:51.330
I've been thinking about it for some time now.

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:54.430
Two rose buds aren't enough to
support the Lady Roses anyway.

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:56.940
You're going to get a little sister for the labor?

00:12:57.510 --> 00:13:00.070
Shimako-san seemed to be against that idea,

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:04.040
but I think taking a practical approach
like that is one way to do it.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:09.280
Besides, I need to diffuse my emotions more...

00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:16.750
Morning.

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:18.690
M-Morning.

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:20.420
How are you feeling?

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:22.960
I'm fine.

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:24.930
I see...

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:35.600
Yoshino.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:39.240
I heard you officially joined the Kendo Team?

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:40.740
Yes.

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:43.640
Basically, your life is your own,

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:47.120
so I have no right to stop you, right?

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:48.450
Rei-chan...

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:51.290
I thought about it a lot while I was away.

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:54.550
About kendo and about you...

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:59.460
And I've had second thoughts
about how we are as sisters.

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:00.590
What?

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:10.110
No matter what, we'll always be
different from normal sisters.

00:14:10.110 --> 00:14:13.170
That's why we end up clashing like this.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.950
That might be true...

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:19.620
Yoshino, as your big sister,

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:22.320
I could persuade you to quit the team.

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:24.650
You mean ask, not persuade, right?

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.320
I suppose, ask...

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:29.990
You might be right...

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:32.660
But you wouldn't acquiesce, right?

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:34.700
I would, if it was right.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:38.440
But your reason for opposing
me isn't compelling.

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:42.800
Why does it end up like this?

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:47.710
Maybe we were wrong to begin
with when we became sisters.

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:52.810
Darn you, Rei-chan! It's all over if you say that!

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:55.350
So, what is it that you're getting at?

00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:59.330
That if you're going to do as you please,

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:01.890
I have to rethink things, too.

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:05.330
I've had enough of being at the
mercy of whatever you decide to do.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:17.210
Face!

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:19.410
Wrist!

00:15:20.950 --> 00:15:23.140
Don't try to go at with just your upper bodies!

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:25.510
Come on! Your legs aren't keeping up!

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:35.090
Rei-chan's still at her coolest
when she's doing kendo.

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:42.400
Yoshi...

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:44.470
Owowow...

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:56.080
What's with that?!

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:12.460
Shall we call it a day soon?

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:16.870
Oh, but I'm almost done
with my regimen for today.

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:18.700
You don't have to strain yourself.

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:20.900
The regimen is just a guideline.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:24.270
Right. You go ahead and go home.

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:26.140
I'll make sure to do the cleaning, too.

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:28.370
I'll help you, so let's go home together.

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:32.450
I'll be fine. I can do it alone.

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:33.580
But...

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:43.490
It looks like it's going rain.

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:44.730
I know.

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:47.660
I'll just work at it for a little longer.

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:50.400
Don't overdo it, okay?

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:51.930
Thanks.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:16:59.250
All right...

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:02.170
I'm not losing!

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:03.910
But... against who?

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:09.750
Against myself?

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:11.650
Or is it against Rei-chan?

00:17:20.570 --> 00:17:21.590
Rain...

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:23.860
No wonder it's cold...

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.170
Not good, not good!

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:44.150
Rei-chan!

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:46.560
I thought you'd gone home already.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:50.830
I was on my way, but I couldn't do it.

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:57.330
I'm not quitting the Kendo Team.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:00.170
I know. I understand your resolve well now.

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:03.370
And you were working hard, too.

00:18:05.550 --> 00:18:08.210
But you don't like it, right?

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:10.240
It's not that I don't like it.

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:11.610
I'm troubled.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.480
What? Troubled?

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:17.620
Yes, troubled and I don't
know what to do with myself.

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:21.260
I guess I was trying to protect my territory.

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:23.260
You mean, the Kendo Team?

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:28.730
How do I look to you when
I'm involved with the team?

00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:30.670
You look really cool!

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:35.140
I actually rather like that about myself.

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:38.950
In that case, I get to see you like that up-close,

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:40.170
so that's good, isn't it?

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:44.280
When you're here, I'm no good.

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:46.620
I lose my composure.

00:18:47.320 --> 00:18:48.150
Rei-chan...

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:51.790
Could you be getting beat up badly?

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:53.890
Could you be getting hurt?

00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:56.050
Those are the only things I can think about.

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:59.090
And I'm hiding that while
I'm training the underclassmen.

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:00.990
I know that.

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:05.270
Because you're kinder than anyone
and more fragile than anyone.

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:08.310
There's no way an inferior person like that...

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:12.370
...could possibly train you along
with the other underclassmen!

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:16.880
I care about the underclassmen,
but you're different.

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:21.520
Just by having to tell myself that
I have to treat you equally,

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:24.150
I'm already being discriminating.

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:28.250
In other words, you're afraid because
you might show me favoritism.

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:33.390
Or that I might treat you harshly in
my attempt not to show favoritism.

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:35.200
I see.

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:36.900
Go ahead and laugh.

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:38.640
I can't laugh at that.

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:55.150
It's okay, you know.
You can turn your back on me now...

00:19:56.390 --> 00:19:57.150
Rei-chan...

00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:13.360
By that, do you mean you want the rosary back?

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:16.500
Right...

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:21.610
Because then, you won't be
at the mercy of whatever I do...

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:25.520
Would you rather have it that way?

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:27.320
Do you not need me anymore?

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:32.310
Of course, I'll always need you!

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:36.020
My feelings for you haven't lessened,
even by one milligram!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:40.630
Rei-chan, if it's for you, I'd do anything.

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:44.500
If you really wanted,
I'd even quit the Kendo Team.

00:20:45.310 --> 00:20:49.870
But you know, if I did that,
I think you'd become even weaker.

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:51.510
And so would I...

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:53.270
Being so dependent on each other...

00:20:56.950 --> 00:20:58.710
I don't want to lose to something like that.

00:20:58.890 --> 00:21:01.480
So I don't want to quit the team right now.

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:04.990
I'm going to work hard at both the
Kendo Team and being a little sister!

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:05.720
That is all!

00:21:21.310 --> 00:21:22.800
You might be right.

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:34.660
What do you want to do?

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:35.920
Should we run to the school building?

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:42.050
It's been left here for a long time,
so I decided to take it.

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:45.520
When it rains, people forget
their umbrellas, I guess.

00:21:59.510 --> 00:22:01.820
I think I might be lucky
that the umbrella's crumpled.

00:22:01.820 --> 00:22:02.710
Why?

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:05.750
Because I get to cling to you,
which I haven't done in a while.

00:22:06.890 --> 00:22:09.820
I think I'll try being at the
mercy of the things you do...

00:22:10.290 --> 00:22:11.420
...for a while longer.

00:23:26.870 --> 00:23:28.940
There are many words for rain.

00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:31.270
Like "downpour," " drizzle," and " squalls."

00:23:31.270 --> 00:23:32.910
"Aoshigure" is early summer rain...

00:23:32.910 --> 00:23:35.180
...and "hisame" is freezing cold winter rain.

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:37.580
"Konuka-ame" is tiny rain that
falls without making a sound...

00:23:37.580 --> 00:23:39.880
...and "teppou-ame" is rain
that pours down furiously.

00:23:39.880 --> 00:23:42.650
There's also "rainstorm,"
"acid rain," and " rain of blood."

00:23:42.650 --> 00:23:44.220
Something's not quite right
about those, Yumi-san.

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:45.220
It sounds kind of dangerous.

00:23:45.220 --> 00:23:46.990
Then, like "harusame" and " arare"?

00:23:46.990 --> 00:23:48.190
They're not wrong, but...

00:23:48.190 --> 00:23:49.350
It's making me hungry.

00:23:49.460 --> 00:23:49.820
Next time on "Maria Watches Over Us,"

00:23:49.820 --> 00:23:51.190
Next time on "Maria Watches Over Us,"
Next Time "Rainy Blue"

00:23:51.190 --> 00:23:52.060
"Rainy Blue".
Next Time "Rainy Blue"

00:23:52.060 --> 00:23:53.430
What kind of rain will it be?
Next Time "Rainy Blue"

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:55.100
Drizzle, drizzle, splish-splash.
Next Time "Rainy Blue"

00:23:55.100 --> 00:23:55.860
Next Time "Rainy Blue"
